I think we were like the normal young  married couple we didn't really fight  about money but they wouldn't talk about  money it was really hard to go from  having controlled all your money to  sharing it with someone else we've been  married for five years and have one  daughter who was born right in the  middle the debt snowball are you doing  if you look up in the doggie yeah how  much dad have you paid off it was a  little over a hundred and forty thousand  dollars but we are here to celebrate  really the last one hundred and twenty  five of that because we did that in  about 30 months and when people ask you  how did you do that what are the secrets  to getting out of that I remember when  we were house hunting we were looking  for houses and I was trying to figure  out how much we could afford per month  and how much our payment was going to be  I was trying to ask her will cabl what  are your monthly payments you know these  are what mine are to see how much we'd  have left after we combined our income  and I remember when she told me you know  well this is my student loan payment I  just was like what do you have how much  in student loan debt before we didn't  talk about it I think on my end there  was a lot of guilt because I came into  the marriage with the student loan debts  like he had a car payment but compared  to the student loan debt it was nothing  so you know I never wanted to bring it  up because I felt guilty like this was  my problem to fix and as I talked to him  about it like it's not his problem we  didn't talk about money that first year  we married because I think that we kind  of both knew that if we did like it  would lead to a fight you know so we  just it was better to just brush it  under the rug and just not think about  it whenever dad came to us and said like  he was going to do the financial peace  class at our church and he'd like us to  go through it with them I think both of  us were like okay we don't need to do  that we're fine we're not having any  issues it wasn't so much I didn't think  we needed it I just didn't want to  uncover all the nasty beasts in our  closet because I knew would force us to  address these issues in my mind I looked  at is something we'll never pay off you  know there's no way this works for  people with thirty forty thousand  dollars in that not 130 the written  budget is absolutely everything because  when we weren't doing the written budget  and giving every dollar a name we  weren't making any progress our money  was just escaping away from us but once  you assigned a adult a name to every  dollar that's when you really start to  make the progress we went through the  class in the spring 2012 and then that  next winter we got art all of our tax  return information I'll never forget my  jaw hit the floor when I opened that  envelope and said we had paid like  twelve thousand dollars interest in one  year and I'm thinking we don't make  enough money to be giving someone twelve  thousand dollars a year like this is  insanity it was kind of at that moment  for me that I looked down I said wow you  know we've got to do something about  this and that's that's when we really  really started to bear down on the  budget and attack this thing with a  vengeance  and then kind of like presented it to me  like if we just buckle down and we do  this the opportunities to do all of  these things open up and so I think that  was the turning point for me mess it up  a lot of shifts as a nurse did yeah a  lot of extra hours a lot of long 12-hour  shifts a lot of time away from my family  but it's worth it because now it's done  every little thing we could find I mean  an extra 20 bucks here and there you  know just everything went straight to  the loan we settled our couch our  kitchen table like pretty much if we  figured we could live without it we sold  it yeah I mean we sold everything in the  house that wasn't nailed down and I was  like okay we've got to get one big last  you know injection into this debt  snowball and so that's when I actually  talked to her the first time about  selling my truck when you sell that nice  truck and move into that 1900 hour car  that right there I'll get you going yeah  that opened some eyes that's I think  that really told people when these guys  are serious we had run the numbers and  it was well within our means to keep it  I thought oh and oh you know we're fine  we don't need sell the truck out of the  truck and then it just kept weighing on  my heart and weighing on my heart and I  kept kind of hearing God tell me like  you need to sell the truck you need to  sell the truck  we just we sold it we got rid of it we  got a really good price for it we just  took all that money I set aside like two  grand so okay I'll buy myself a new car  with this and then the rest of it you  know  Wham we made a big day and that was just  it was just all downhill from there now  that we're debt-free and we look back  you know it's kind of hard to believe  and now we can start saving that money  and investing it for our future and for  our daughter's future and from here on  out like our kids are going to grow up  not ever having to worry about life 3 2  1 we're damn free
 

